From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] texture_cache: a large device may fill 5/8 of its budget before collecting

Ported from Frizti/Fritchii 78f38e077 (zortos293/Lichii #268), which Fritchii carries in v5.

The collector's thresholds are sized for a device with far less memory than this one presents. The PS5
reports a ~6 GiB Vulkan budget, and our own logs show the heap driven to 6274 of 6422 MiB - 98% -
while the collector keeps evicting: 2633 images created and 3615 deleted in a single 600-frame window,
with the present frame time doubling from 32 ms to 61 ms. Collecting that hard, that early, is what
makes the churn, because the cache throws away images it is about to need again.

Fritchii lets a large card fill 5/8 of its budget before it collects at all, so the working set a big
scene needs can stay resident.

What this can break: a device filling 5/8 of its budget keeps less headroom for one large allocation,
so a big texture arriving into a full cache has a narrower window between "fits" and "fails". That is
why it belongs with 0427, which makes a texture that does not fit fail cleanly instead of being left
unbacked - the two are a pair.

Measured or a guess: the churn counts and heap percentages are from our own log, and the threshold
change is measured on upstream's hardware. The effect on the PS5 is not console-tested.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index adda3a859..315177c31 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -408,10 +408,18 @@ bool TextureCache<P>::IsAllStale(DAddr addr, size_t size) const {
 
 template <class P>
 void TextureCache<P>::ApplyThresholdOverrides(bool log) {
-    // On every GPU: past what a frame needs, more device memory only keeps the textures of earlier
-    // scenes (title 1 filled 6.7 GB of an 8 GB card and draws its races in ~5 GB), so collect from
-    // MaxCriticalMemory on rather than near the card's budget.
-    critical_memory = (std::min)(critical_memory, MaxCriticalMemory);
+    // Past what a frame needs, more device memory only keeps the textures of earlier scenes
+    // (title 1 filled 6.7 GB of an 8 GB card and draws its races in ~5 GB), so collect from
+    // MaxCriticalMemory on rather than near the card's budget. Larger cards get 5/8 of the
+    // driver's budget (GetDeviceLocalMemory is capped near 7 GiB): at 5 GiB title 1's races
+    // recreate and upload ~8 MiB of render targets a frame (16 GB card: 53 -> 59 fps at 10 GiB).
+    // 5/8 of the budget only passes 5 GiB above an 8 GiB budget, so cards up to 8 GB (and
+    // integrated GPUs, whose budget is capped at 4-6 GiB) keep the 5 GiB cap.
+    u64 max_critical = MaxCriticalMemory;
+    if constexpr (requires { runtime.GetDeviceMemoryBudget(); }) {
+        max_critical = (std::max)(max_critical, runtime.GetDeviceMemoryBudget() / 8 * 5);
+    }
+    critical_memory = (std::min)(critical_memory, max_critical);
     expected_memory =
         (std::min)(expected_memory, critical_memory - (std::min)(critical_memory, u64{768_MiB}));
     minimum_memory =
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index 29c42fcf4..1faf9e21f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -152,8 +152,8 @@ class TextureCache : public VideoCommon::ChannelSetupCaches<TextureCacheChannelI
 
     static constexpr s64 DEFAULT_EXPECTED_MEMORY = 1_GiB + 125_MiB;
     static constexpr s64 DEFAULT_CRITICAL_MEMORY = 1_GiB + 625_MiB;
-    /// The most device memory the collector lets the cache fill before it collects in earnest,
-    /// on every GPU (ApplyThresholdOverrides).
+    /// The most device memory the collector lets the cache fill before it collects in earnest on
+    /// cards up to 8 GiB; larger ones 5/8 of the driver's budget (ApplyThresholdOverrides).
     static constexpr u64 MaxCriticalMemory = 5_GiB;
     static constexpr size_t GC_EMERGENCY_COUNTS = 2;
 
